/E (Coal mining is one of the most hazardous occupations in the industrial world. Miners are continuously exposed to potential dangers such as toxic gases \(methane, carbon monoxide\), poor lighting, high humidity, and the risk of accidents due to falls or collapses. Traditional helmets offer only physical protection and fail to provide real-time feedback on environmental and physical conditions. )
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [1]
